  Turnover is the number to read first. A conviction strategy that churns
  has failed regardless of its return: it is back in the regime where the
  evidence says trading costs eat the edge, which is where every price-based
  strategy in this project has already died.

  These are backtests on survivorship-biased data — 7,062 delisted companies
  are absent — and the value screens shop among cheap, distressed-looking
  names, which is exactly where that bias is worst. Treat as ranking, not
  forecast, and read bias_exposure.py alongside.
